cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "fewlab: fewest items to label for most efficient unbiased OLS on shares"
version: 4.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-24"
url: "https://github.com/finite-sample/fewlab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/finite-sample/fewlab"
authors:
- family-names: "Sood"
  given-names: "Gaurav"
abstract: "Chooses which reusable entity labels to buy so that a downstream regression is as precise as possible without giving up unbiasedness. The complete-label coefficient decomposes exactly as a sum of per-entity contributions, which fixes each entity's value before any label is purchased and yields the risk-minimizing inclusion probabilities, a certainty core that falls out of the budget constraint, and design-based standard errors."
keywords:
  - "survey sampling"
  - "Horvitz-Thompson"
  - "optimal design"
  - "unequal probability sampling"
  - "regression analysis"
  - "active learning"
  - "annotation"
license: MIT
